WEBVTT

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:03.480
<b>Angel of Murder</b>

00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:14.950
Genetic code confirmed. Key level 3 unlock.

00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:22.880
Hey, rookie, is dinner ready yet?

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:24.010
Almost!

00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:24.960
Sheesh.

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:28.860
Why do I gotta cook 
for my own welcoming party?

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:32.570
Yay! Victory is mine!

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:32.840
<b>WINNER WINNER CHICKEN DINNER</b>

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:34.360
Damn, you got me!

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:36.220
I can't believe you beat Kondo at shooting.

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:38.320
I'm a gamer at heart, you see.

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:40.110
Okay, all done.

00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:43.340
Oh, right. I've taken over Alma's body 
a bunch of times now.

00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:46.780
I never really had time 
to dwell on it before,

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:49.260
but you know...

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:52.190
Let's eat!

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:55.530
What the heck? This is amazing!

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:56.920
Yeah, it's yummy!

00:00:56.920 --> 00:00:58.820
We got a master chef in the house, baby.

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:01.000
Way to go, kid.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:03.880
I'm glad you like it. And thanks, Alma.

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:06.320
<i>Don't mention it. Connecting with you,</i>

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:09.230
<i>your actions, and your thoughts 
is a valuable experience.</i>

00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:12.800
<i>It must be because you're human, 
and not an AI like myself.</i>

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:15.370
"Human," huh...

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:16.970
Yum!

00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:18.490
Is something the matter?

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:22.060
This is so good.

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:25.310
I never realized how amazing 
my senses were until I lost them.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:27.560
Akira...

00:01:29.810 --> 00:01:34.730
Will I ever go back to being human?

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:37.990
Chief?

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:41.320
<i>All hands, listen up. 
We have orders to sortie.</i>

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:17.670
An individual taking asylum in Japan 
is suspected of possessing an EX-ARM.

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:19.170
Asylum?

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:24.170
Correct. The former president 
of the Mwange Republic, Jason Mraw.

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:27.530
President Mraw... You mean that guy?

00:03:27.530 --> 00:03:30.810
The dictator who carried out 
the Mwange Genocide four years ago?

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:33.690
What's that "Mwange Genocide" thing?

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:37.050
Well, obviously, uh... What was it, again?

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:38.840
You don't know, either?!

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:40.570
This squad sure has gained new life.

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:43.310
Superintendent, switch to the archive.

00:03:43.310 --> 00:03:44.910
In 2026,

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:48.870
Mraw, then the president-cum-dictator 
of the Mwange Republic in Africa,

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:52.110
was looking to found a new nation 
for androids.

00:03:52.110 --> 00:03:54.300
When the people opposed it,

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:58.380
he used his android troops 
and his EX-ARM to massacre them.

00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:02.130
Here's some footage we've obtained 
of the incident.

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:03.690
What was that?

00:04:03.690 --> 00:04:05.660
Their heads disappeared?

00:04:06.210 --> 00:04:10.510
Erasing spaces like that is something 
modern science can't decipher.

00:04:10.510 --> 00:04:11.690
Which means...

00:04:11.690 --> 00:04:13.980
An EX-ARM was involved.

00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:16.150
That's so cruel.

00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:19.850
The ensuing civil war led 
to the overthrow of the Mraw regime,

00:04:19.850 --> 00:04:23.130
and he sought asylum in Japan.

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:34.920
This is the Bibot used by the militaries 
of most major European countries.

00:04:35.510 --> 00:04:38.780
Ordinary firearms can't even scratch 
this fine piece of work.

00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:41.260
Excellent as always from Hanoi Farm.

00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:43.590
I'm your man when it comes to weapons.

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:47.390
I'm sure Master Mraw will be quite pleased 
with this purchase.

00:04:48.820 --> 00:04:54.900
And our country accepted him, knowing that 
the decision would be slammed worldwide.

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:56.690
Who's the girl?

00:04:56.690 --> 00:04:58.330
Her name's Elmira.

00:04:58.330 --> 00:05:01.240
She's an android, and Mraw's personal maid.

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:04.710
There's talk that 
she helped with the genocide.

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:09.950
We didn't build her, so her specs are unknown. 
Gotta watch out for her.

00:05:09.950 --> 00:05:13.520
Y'know, why'd we even let this asshole in?

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:15.290
Diplomatic reasons.

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:18.220
By helping Mraw,

00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:21.770
the US could cheaply procure rare metals 
from companies with ties to him.

00:05:21.770 --> 00:05:25.450
They wanted the booze, but not the boos.

00:05:25.450 --> 00:05:27.850
So they forced Japan to take him instead.

00:05:27.850 --> 00:05:29.260
That sucks!

00:05:29.690 --> 00:05:33.080
That said, there was plenty of opposition 
to it within Japan as well,

00:05:33.080 --> 00:05:38.440
so the government decided to make him 
live in the Yokosuka SEZ.

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:40.440
<b>Yokosuka SEZ</b>

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:40.440
"S... E... Z"?

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:43.960
It's like a little foreign nation 
within Japan.

00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:48.140
The UN military's stationed there, 
and extraterritorial rights are in effect.

00:05:48.140 --> 00:05:50.780
Cops like us can't do shit there.

00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:57.960
But if Mraw has an EX-ARM, 
it's our job to confiscate it.

00:05:57.960 --> 00:06:02.440
So we're going to investigate 
his mansion undercover.

00:06:02.440 --> 00:06:04.090
Undercover?

00:06:04.090 --> 00:06:07.130
The ones on this mission 
will be you and Alma,

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:08.720
Number 00.

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:10.090
Who, me?!

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:14.710
You'll use your hacking capabilities 
to back up Alma.

00:06:15.170 --> 00:06:16.900
Just so you know,

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:20.230
everyone who's gone to investigate that mansion

00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:22.630
has gone MIA.

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:28.170
His EX-ARM's ability may have
something to do with it.

00:06:28.170 --> 00:06:31.070
Confiscate it before other countries catch on.

00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:32.560
Understood.

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:34.960
One second! That place sounds dangerous!

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:37.100
Sending this idiot would be one thing, 
but Alma, too?

00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:38.350
Don't call me an idiot!

00:06:38.350 --> 00:06:40.310
Minami, a mission is a mission.

00:06:42.260 --> 00:06:45.630
Genetic code confirmed. Key level 3 unlock.

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:51.670
Excuse me, Master Mraw.

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:56.140
I'll leave your drink here.

00:06:57.100 --> 00:06:59.500
What were you gazing at?

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:07.640
So this is the SEZ.

00:07:07.640 --> 00:07:09.490
What, first time here?

00:07:10.840 --> 00:07:14.870
That guy's UN Lieutenant Neville, 
the guy in charge around here.

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:20.100
Yo. I hope you didn't come 'ere 
to corrupt this fresh young rookie.

00:07:20.660 --> 00:07:26.260
Surely it can't be that 
Japanese cops are here on duty, right?

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:28.280
Actually, it is.

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:30.160
Let us through.

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:33.420
I'll let you off the hook 
'cause you get slave wages,

00:07:33.420 --> 00:07:36.720
but next time you wanna go through, 
bring me a souvenir.

00:07:38.550 --> 00:07:40.890
He's such a jerk. Every time.

00:07:40.890 --> 00:07:43.150
But now we don't need an appointment.

00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:45.240
Our guy must've heard by now.

00:07:45.240 --> 00:07:47.720
Um, who are going to meet?

00:07:47.720 --> 00:07:50.780
The guy who knows this town 
like the back of his hand.

00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:54.620
<b>Hanoi Farm</b>

00:07:52.260 --> 00:07:54.120
Well, well.

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:57.620
Welcome to my office.

00:07:58.600 --> 00:08:01.370
What could the police want from me?

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:05.100
You're the go-to guy 
for information in this town.

00:08:05.100 --> 00:08:07.200
As they say, it takes one to know one.

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:10.630
I'll have to hear your questions first, 
before I decide whether to answer.

00:08:12.690 --> 00:08:16.950
You know Mraw, the guy who took asylum here 
from the Mwange Republic, don't you?

00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:24.600
<i>Y'know, what's with this tight-ass outfit?</i>

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:27.040
<i>It's a bodysuit specced for stealth missions.</i>

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:30.250
<i>It won't show up on radar, 
as long as it doesn't get destroyed.</i>

00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:36.820
<i>If it does, it'll send an SOS to Squad HQ.</i>

00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:38.830
<i>Destroyed?</i>

00:08:38.830 --> 00:08:41.360
<i>I sure hope it doesn't come to that.</i>

00:08:41.360 --> 00:08:44.620
<i>Let's sneak into the mansion 
and look for Mraw.</i>

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:45.750
<i>Okay!</i>

00:08:48.600 --> 00:08:50.140
<i>But man...</i>

00:08:50.140 --> 00:08:55.130
<i>Androids were still a sci-fi concept 
back in my day.</i>

00:08:55.130 --> 00:08:58.300
<i>Come to think of it, 
my brother was researching them.</i>

00:08:58.720 --> 00:09:04.600
<i>Android technology hit a major breakthrough 
in the latter half of the '10s.</i>

00:09:04.910 --> 00:09:08.220
<i>The research team that'd later spawn 
Iriya Heavy Industries</i>

00:09:08.220 --> 00:09:10.820
<i>published a revolutionary theory.</i>

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:16.410
<i>After the Tokyo Attack, we were mass-produced 
to help rescue and repair efforts,</i>

00:09:16.410 --> 00:09:18.110
<i>and we grew rapidly in number.</i>

00:09:18.110 --> 00:09:21.260
<i>A worldwide market for androids 
sprang up overnight.</i>

00:09:22.100 --> 00:09:23.610
<i>Oh...</i>

00:09:23.610 --> 00:09:30.090
<i>But the biggest factor in getting androids 
to this point was the military-industrial complex</i>

00:09:30.090 --> 00:09:36.130
<i>with its R&D on using androids as weapons 
or tools to replace manual labor.</i>

00:09:36.430 --> 00:09:39.080
<i>As we quickly gained a foothold in society,</i>

00:09:39.080 --> 00:09:44.760
<i>we also became a target of criticism 
and hatred for taking human jobs and status.</i>

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:50.680
Oh. That kinda sucks.

00:09:50.680 --> 00:09:51.920
What does?

00:09:51.920 --> 00:09:53.340
You have to ask?

00:09:53.340 --> 00:09:55.200
There's no problem at all.

00:09:55.200 --> 00:09:59.820
We are tools built to serve humanity.

00:10:04.310 --> 00:10:11.210
A company truck of yours was spotted 
transporting something to Mraw's mansion.

00:10:11.960 --> 00:10:14.040
What did you sell him?

00:10:14.710 --> 00:10:16.420
Whatever could you mean?

00:10:16.420 --> 00:10:18.420
You're an arms dealer.

00:10:18.420 --> 00:10:23.740
I bet you badly want to get your hands 
on Mraw's EX-ARM, right?

00:10:23.740 --> 00:10:27.480
So what are you plotting? Answer us.

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:30.940
You want the EX-ARM as badly as I do.

00:10:30.940 --> 00:10:32.840
Which makes you a business rival.

00:10:32.840 --> 00:10:34.820
I have nothing to say to you.

00:10:35.210 --> 00:10:36.620
Please leave.

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:41.160
I'm sure we'll be seeing 
each other again very soon.

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:45.300
It's me.

00:10:49.060 --> 00:10:52.020
<i>Man, this is one huge place.</i>

00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:56.320
<i>There's a room we can't analyze down here.</i>

00:10:56.320 --> 00:10:57.380
<i>Gotcha.</i>

00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:01.200
<i>Can't see a thing. Get the lights.</i>

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:10.970
Screw Nguyen and his pompous ass!

00:11:10.970 --> 00:11:13.180
He's definitely involved.

00:11:13.180 --> 00:11:15.420
I'm worried about 
whatever weapon he sold Mraw.

00:11:15.420 --> 00:11:18.510
Will Alma and Akira be okay?

00:11:18.510 --> 00:11:19.780
Let's head to the mansion.

00:11:22.710 --> 00:11:24.480
What's with these things?!

00:11:24.480 --> 00:11:26.160
They're the UN's Hounds.

00:11:26.160 --> 00:11:28.670
<i>This is the UN military.</i>

00:11:28.670 --> 00:11:31.400
<i>Put your weapons down immediately.</i>

00:11:31.400 --> 00:11:34.540
<i>If you don't comply, 
you will be shot on the spot.</i>

00:11:35.530 --> 00:11:37.420
Neville!

00:11:37.420 --> 00:11:40.130
I hate to tell you, but you're
not getting anywhere near Mraw.

00:11:40.130 --> 00:11:42.680
In this town, I am the law. Got that?

00:11:43.480 --> 00:11:46.140
Turn your ass around, 
and get out of the SEZ!

00:11:50.050 --> 00:11:52.330
<i>What's with this room?</i>

00:11:56.450 --> 00:12:00.740
<i>It's likely that most of them are victims 
of the Mwange Genocide.</i>

00:12:03.720 --> 00:12:05.860
I didn't realize we had guests.

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:10.040
You're Elmira, right?

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:11.960
Indeed. And you are?

00:12:12.300 --> 00:12:13.900
Japanese police!

00:12:13.900 --> 00:12:15.380
Where is Mraw?

00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:18.470
Master Mraw is busy at the moment.

00:12:19.240 --> 00:12:21.080
What's all this, then?

00:12:21.080 --> 00:12:23.430
Android face samples.

00:12:24.130 --> 00:12:25.550
Why would you do this?

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:30.520
To make Mwange a truly
beautiful, peaceful utopia.

00:12:31.850 --> 00:12:35.110
I shall eliminate anyone 
who gets in Master Mraw's way.

00:12:41.460 --> 00:12:43.720
<i>It disappeared? Was that...</i>

00:12:43.720 --> 00:12:47.160
<i>This makes no sense. 
Only humans should be able to use EX-ARMs.</i>

00:12:52.440 --> 00:12:55.050
<i>Back off and let me handle this, Akira!</i>

00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:09.850
<i>Hold up, Alma! What's the point
of fighting between androids?</i>

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:12.680
<i>It doesn't matter. 
We function only as programmed.</i>

00:13:23.990 --> 00:13:26.890
I'm sure Elmira would say the same, huh?

00:13:26.890 --> 00:13:28.730
But I don't want to fight her.

00:13:29.380 --> 00:13:33.540
If I can connect to her, I think I
can confirm how she can use an EX-ARM.

00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:34.740
<i>Got it.</i>

00:13:34.740 --> 00:13:35.330
<i>In that case...</i>

00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:37.750
Oh? Trying to connect to me, are we?

00:14:05.610 --> 00:14:07.080
Akira! Alma!

00:14:07.080 --> 00:14:09.500
Minami and the guys are in trouble! 
Back them up!

00:14:10.100 --> 00:14:12.490
Shit! We were almost there!

00:14:14.720 --> 00:14:15.460
Okay.

00:14:16.020 --> 00:14:17.210
I understand.

00:14:17.210 --> 00:14:21.610
Master Mraw, we must prepare to depart.

00:14:22.960 --> 00:14:24.960
<b>Illustration by Komi Shinya</b>

00:14:27.970 --> 00:14:31.460
We received the contribution request 
from Cabinet Secretary Kido.

00:14:32.070 --> 00:14:33.850
You seem to be going through a rough patch.

00:14:35.810 --> 00:14:38.920
I mean, you used to loathe EX-ARMs so much,

00:14:38.920 --> 00:14:42.020
and now you have Number 00 
as part of your squad?

00:14:42.350 --> 00:14:45.450
Fight fire with fire, as they say.

00:14:46.290 --> 00:14:48.530
Well, I sure hope you can put up a fight.

00:14:49.120 --> 00:14:55.100
Mraw, the dictator who took asylum here 
from Mwange, is involved in this case.

00:14:55.100 --> 00:14:57.040
That explains the Yokosuka SEZ.

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:05.080
Are you really going to use this thing?

00:15:05.080 --> 00:15:08.760
Yes. We need it immediately.

00:15:11.830 --> 00:15:14.140
Superintendent! Can you hear me?!

00:15:14.140 --> 00:15:16.650
We're being attacked by the UN military!

00:15:16.650 --> 00:15:18.640
<i>Don't fire until we get approval.</i>

00:15:18.640 --> 00:15:21.940
<i>Akira and Alma are headed your way 
to provide backup.</i>

00:15:25.150 --> 00:15:29.210
Come on! Why can't we get in touch 
with the chief now, of all times?!

00:15:29.690 --> 00:15:30.860
Chief?

00:15:30.860 --> 00:15:32.480
Where are you now?

00:15:32.480 --> 00:15:33.620
<i>Iriya Heavy Industries.</i>

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:36.740
<i>I've arranged for additional equipment.</i>

00:15:38.400 --> 00:15:40.090
"Additional equipment"?

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:46.840
<i>For six hours starting now,</i>

00:15:46.840 --> 00:15:49.550
<i>I am approving the use 
of firearms in the SEZ.</i>

00:15:49.550 --> 00:15:51.220
We can finally shoot back!

00:15:59.780 --> 00:16:04.480
Our hound dogs ain't gonna go down 
to such weak fire.

00:16:06.550 --> 00:16:09.360
Damn it! We stand no chance like this!

00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:17.660
<i>Hang in there until the
additional equipment arrives.</i>

00:16:17.660 --> 00:16:18.700
<i>Over and out.</i>

00:16:19.920 --> 00:16:21.500
Easier said than done!

00:16:32.150 --> 00:16:33.000
Alma!

00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:33.840
Akira?

00:16:33.840 --> 00:16:34.780
Behind you!

00:16:40.160 --> 00:16:43.450
What's this additional equipment 
Chief Shiga's talking about?

00:16:43.450 --> 00:16:45.270
How should I know?

00:17:11.550 --> 00:17:13.790
Whoa! What the hell is that?

00:17:13.790 --> 00:17:15.050
A Bibot!

00:17:16.770 --> 00:17:20.930
It's a little cramped in here, 
but I hope you'll endure it, Master Mraw.

00:17:21.590 --> 00:17:25.100
I shall take you to a whole new world very soon.

00:17:38.780 --> 00:17:40.070
<i>Is that Elmira?</i>

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:44.730
An escape?

00:17:45.840 --> 00:17:49.360
If they keep going, they'll hit the UN base,

00:17:49.360 --> 00:17:52.670
which has transport planes 
they can steal to leave the country.

00:17:52.670 --> 00:17:58.110
They might be planning to leave Japan 
and then do business with Hanoi Farm.

00:17:52.920 --> 00:18:02.680
<b>Yokosuka SEZ</b>

00:17:52.920 --> 00:18:02.680
<b>UN Military Base</b>

00:17:58.110 --> 00:18:00.820
So that's what Nguyen was after!

00:18:04.980 --> 00:18:09.040
That Bibot can kick the UN's
little pups to the curb.

00:18:09.040 --> 00:18:12.730
Now, I'll leave the dogfight to them.

00:18:15.120 --> 00:18:17.230
To the unscathed go the spoils.

00:18:17.230 --> 00:18:19.950
As long as we have the last laugh, 
that's all that matters.

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:22.760
What the hell?

00:18:22.760 --> 00:18:27.090
Damn it, Nguyen! 
Isn't that the Bibot you sold him?!

00:18:27.090 --> 00:18:29.040
<i>Warning! Warning!</i>

00:18:31.400 --> 00:18:32.520
<i>Uh...</i>

00:18:32.520 --> 00:18:34.720
<i>This is the UN military.</i>

00:18:34.720 --> 00:18:37.840
<i>Mister Mraw! His name is Mraw, right?</i>

00:18:37.840 --> 00:18:42.310
<i>You must know you aren't allowed 
to leave the premises of your residence.</i>

00:18:43.830 --> 00:18:44.760
Look!

00:18:45.120 --> 00:18:46.780
The additional equipment!

00:18:48.530 --> 00:18:52.070
<i>Disarm yourself and surrender at once!</i>

00:18:52.550 --> 00:18:54.400
<i>If you don't comply...</i>

00:18:54.960 --> 00:18:56.900
...this is what will happen.

00:19:20.450 --> 00:19:21.980
No! The trailer!

00:19:23.400 --> 00:19:24.440
Shit!

00:19:27.590 --> 00:19:31.640
"Eliminate all the nuisances," yes?

00:19:31.640 --> 00:19:34.230
I'm aware, Master Mraw.

00:19:37.200 --> 00:19:38.700
Stop it, Elmira!

00:19:39.670 --> 00:19:40.600
Akira!

00:19:49.650 --> 00:19:52.780
Why would you drag random people into this?

00:19:52.780 --> 00:19:54.080
<i>I believe I told you.</i>

00:19:54.680 --> 00:19:57.480
<i>It's because those are Master Mraw's orders.</i>

00:19:57.480 --> 00:19:59.690
You'll follow any order 
without questioning it?!

00:19:59.690 --> 00:20:03.520
<i>That is what we were created for.</i>

00:20:03.520 --> 00:20:06.120
<i>Besides, there is more to it.</i>

00:20:07.750 --> 00:20:10.680
Master Mraw made me a promise.

00:20:10.680 --> 00:20:12.310
A promise, to an android like me.

00:20:13.250 --> 00:20:14.600
<i>A promise?</i>

00:20:15.940 --> 00:20:18.780
Anyone who gets in our way will pay.

00:20:22.240 --> 00:20:24.820
<i>Focus on hacking, Akira.</i>

00:20:26.200 --> 00:20:27.190
<i>Got it!</i>

00:20:28.660 --> 00:20:31.230
<i>Is there anything I can log into?</i>

00:20:31.230 --> 00:20:34.080
<i>Car, robot, anything will do!</i>

00:20:35.270 --> 00:20:36.420
<i>Nope.</i>

00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:37.930
<i>This won't work.</i>

00:20:37.930 --> 00:20:40.740
<i>Damn it! They're all fighting out there!</i>

00:20:41.330 --> 00:20:42.810
<i>Screw this!</i>

00:20:42.810 --> 00:20:47.080
<i>Am I going to be powerless to help yet again?</i>

00:20:45.970 --> 00:20:47.930
<b>Akira</b>

00:20:47.080 --> 00:20:47.930
Akira.

00:20:49.470 --> 00:20:51.890
<b>Can you take another step forward?</b>

00:20:49.470 --> 00:20:51.890
Can you take another step forward, Akira?

00:20:56.920 --> 00:20:57.990
Akira.

00:20:59.990 --> 00:21:02.030
You've just gotta put your best foot forward.

00:21:03.320 --> 00:21:04.550
Bro...

00:21:15.160 --> 00:21:16.250
Alma!

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:17.260
Minami!

00:21:20.210 --> 00:21:21.380
Alma!

00:23:25.760 --> 00:23:29.150
An android's only purpose is to obey orders.

00:23:29.150 --> 00:23:30.760
That is what I have always believed.

00:23:30.760 --> 00:23:32.470
Just like her.

00:23:32.470 --> 00:23:36.000
Next time, on <i>EX-ARM:</i> 
"Battle 004 - Inheritor of Courage."

00:23:34.530 --> 00:23:39.970
<b>Inheritor of Courage</b>

00:23:36.000 --> 00:23:38.430
Why is this tearing my heart apart 
when I don't have one?
